  "raw": {
    "https://www.carthage.edu/live/news/58129-visiting-assistant-professor-physics": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Physics",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Physics • Human Resources • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Visiting Assistant Professor, Physics Home Human Resources Visiting Assistant Professor, Physics All Stories October 13, 2026 Dr. Jean Quashnock at physics-search@carthage.edu Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on LinkedIn Share via Email The Department of Physics & Astronomy at Carthage College is seeking applicants for a visiting instructional faculty member beginning in February 2027. This role primarily focuses on teaching introductory algebra- and calculus-based physics sequences to support growing student enrollment in pre-health and engineering pathways. Candidates must hold at least a master’s degree in physics or a related field (Ph.D. strongly preferred). The teaching load includes 3 lectures and 1 lab section per semester, along with 1 course during the January term. To apply, submit a single PDF containing your cover letter, CV, a statement of teaching philosophy, and contact details for three professional references. The cover letter should highlight your experience with introductory physics sequences and your interest in joining a small liberal arts college community. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, but full consideration will be given to those submitted by November 15, 2026. Address any questions to Dr. Jean Quashnock at physics-search@carthage.edu. More information about the Carthage College Department of Physics & Astronomy may be found at http://www.carthage.edu/physics/ Minimum Qualifications Masters in Physics or closely related field Commitment to best pedagogical practices in physics education Experience teaching undergraduate physics desirable Enthusiasm for educating students from widely varying backgrounds Desire to relocate or commute to Kenosha, WI Green card or US citizenship Apply Online About Carthage Located on the shore of Lake Michigan in the thriving Chicago-Milwaukee corridor, Carthage College blends the best liberal arts traditions with desirable degree programs, transformative learning opportunities, and personal attention from dedicated faculty and staff. Our beautiful campus, an 80-acre arboretum with stunning lake views, is home to 2,600 undergraduate students and 200 graduate students. Founded in 1847, Carthage is consistently named a Best Midwestern College by The Princeton Review and a Most Innovative School by U.S. News & World Report. All Carthage employees play a vital part in the success of our students, as we work together to create an environment where all can achieve their true potential. Grow with Carthage. Carthage College is an equal opportunity employer (EOE) dedicated to the goal of building a culturally diverse community. We welcome applications from a broad spectrum of people, including members of ethnic minorities, women, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender expression, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, protected veteran status or status as an individual with a disability. 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    },
    "https://www.carthage.edu/live/news/58037-assistant-professor-finance": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Finance",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Finance • Human Resources • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Assistant Professor, Finance Home Human Resources Assistant Professor, Finance All Stories September 28, 2026 Chao Zheng; czheng@carthage.edu Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on LinkedIn Share via Email The Finance Department at Carthage College invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Finance position on a multi-year renewable contract, starting Fall 2027. The successful candidate will join the Finance Department to teach undergraduate finance courses that may include Corporate Finance, Money & Banking, Security Analysis & Portfolio Management, and Fixed Income & Derivatives Analysis, depending on departmental needs and the candidate’s expertise. The candidate will also play a key role in shaping career-preparation coursework, with the opportunity to design new courses aligned with the CFA and/or CFP curricula, and to help the Department expand its offerings in fintech and AI applications in finance. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree (or higher) in Finance or a related field from an AACSB-accredited institution Significant professional experience in investment, banking, or another area of financial services Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in Finance or a related field Evidence of prior teaching effectiveness in a liberal arts setting Experience with or interest in fintech, financial data analytics, or AI applications in finance, and the ability to help build this area into the curriculum Established relationships with employers, alumni, or industry professionals that can support student career outcomes In addition to teaching, the successful candidate will serve as faculty advisor to the Finance and Investment Club, collaborate with employers, alumni, and career readiness staff to keep the curriculum industry-relevant, and provide service to the college and department through advising and committee work. Interested candidates should submit a single PDF file including a cover letter, curriculum vitae, evidence of past teaching effectiveness, and the names and contact information of three professional references. For best consideration, applications should be received by 11/30. Additional questions about this position can be directed to Dr. Chao Zheng, Chair of the Finance Department, at czheng@carthage.edu. Apply Online About Carthage Located on the shore of Lake Michigan in the thriving Chicago-Milwaukee corridor, Carthage College blends the best liberal arts traditions with desirable degree programs, transformative learning opportunities, and personal attention from dedicated faculty and staff. Our beautiful campus, an 80-acre arboretum with stunning lake views, is home to 2,600 undergraduate students and 200 graduate students. Founded in 1847, Carthage is consistently named a Best Midwestern College by The Princeton Review and a Most Innovative School by U.S. News & World Report. All Carthage employees play a vital part in the success of our students, as we work together to create an environment where all can achieve their true potential. Grow with Carthage. Carthage College is an equal opportunity employer (EOE) dedicated to the goal of building a culturally diverse community. We welcome applications from a broad spectrum of people, including members of ethnic minorities, women, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender expression, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, protected veteran status or status as an individual with a disability. 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    },
    "https://www.carthage.edu/live/news/57985-assistant-professor-of-education-ccsee-bilingual": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Education - CCSEE, Bilingual, or Early Childhood • Human Resources • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Assistant Professor of Education - CCSEE, Bilingual, or Early Childhood Home Human Resources Assistant Professor of Education - CCSEE, Bilingual, or Early Childhood All Stories September 17, 2026 Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on LinkedIn Share via Email The Carthage College Department of Education seeks an Assistant Professor of Education. This is a full-time, benefits-eligible contract (non-tenure) position. We seek a highly qualified and versatile faculty member with interdisciplinary licensure expertise to support and expand innovative teacher preparation pathways. The department is committed to preparing future educators who can skillfully serve diverse populations by integrating strong pedagogy with culturally responsive, non-biased, and empathetic approaches to teaching and learning. We provide both undergraduate and graduate pathways to licensure as well as a Master’s in Education program. Primary Responsibilities Teach general courses for all education students as well as within a specific license area such as CCSE, Bilingual/ Bicultural, or Early Childhood Education Teach graduate courses as needed/able in a hyflex synchronous/asynchronous format Lead or contribute to program innovation in high-need certification areas Participate in departmental service and program leadership initiatives Required Qualifications PhD or EdD in Education or related field, but will consider a Master’s degree with significant experience Demonstrated expertise in any of the following areas: CCSE (Cross-Categorical Special Education) Bilingual /Bicultural (BL/BC) Early Childhood Education P–12 teaching experience Preferred Qualifications Experience working across multiple grade bands or licensure areas Experience with program design, interdisciplinary teaching, or clinical partnerships Leadership experience in schools or educator preparation programs All applicants should complete the online application at www.carthage.edu. Applicants must include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and a list of three current professional references. Apply Online About Carthage Located on the shore of Lake Michigan in the thriving Chicago-Milwaukee corridor, Carthage College blends the best liberal arts traditions with desirable degree programs, transformative learning opportunities, and personal attention from dedicated faculty and staff. Our beautiful campus, an 80-acre arboretum with stunning lake views, is home to 2,600 undergraduate students and 200 graduate students. Founded in 1847, Carthage is consistently named a Best Midwestern College by The Princeton Review and a Most Innovative School by U.S. News & World Report. All Carthage employees play a vital part in the success of our students, as we work together to create an environment where all can achieve their true potential. Grow with Carthage. Carthage College is an equal opportunity employer (EOE) dedicated to the goal of building a culturally diverse community. We welcome applications from a broad spectrum of people, including members of ethnic minorities, women, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender expression, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, protected veteran status or status as an individual with a disability. 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    },
