    "https://www.carthage.edu/live/news/56921-visiting-assistant-professor-mathematics": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Mathematics",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Mathematics • Human Resources • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Visiting Assistant Professor, Mathematics Home Human Resources Visiting Assistant Professor, Mathematics All Stories September 17, 2026 Dr. Haley Yaple; math-search@carthage.edu Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on LinkedIn Share via Email The Mathematics Department at Carthage College invites applicants for a two-year non-renewable position as Visiting Assistant Professor of Mathematics, with an anticipated start date of February 1st, 2026. The successful candidate will teach a variety of introductory-level mathematics courses, including the calculus sequence and statistics. Carthage faculty have recently developed alternatives for some of these standard courses; such innovation in course design and pedagogy is welcomed. Other teaching assignments will depend on departmental needs and candidate specialty; flexibility to teach across the mathematics and data science curriculum, including at the general education level, is desired. The expected teaching load is 32 credits or generally eight four-credit courses per year, one of which may take place during our intensive January term. Carthage’s Math Department offers majors in Mathematics and Data Science and supports students in programs across the college, including a new engineering program. More information about our department may be found at http://www.carthage.edu/mathematics/ . Interested candidates should submit a single PDF file including a cover letter, curriculum vitae, 1–3 page statement of teaching philosophy, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Additional questions about this position can be directed to Dr. Haley Yaple at math-search@carthage.edu . For best consideration, applications should be received by October 16, 2026. Minimum Qualifications: M.S. in Mathematics (or a related mathematical science such as Applied Mathematics, Statistics, Data Science, or Mathematics Education) by January 2027 required ; Ph.D. preferred. Demonstrated record of or potential for successful undergraduate mathematics instruction Demonstrated interest in effective mathematics teaching and continual improvement of pedagogical practices Enthusiasm for supporting and improving diversity, equity, and inclusion in the classroom Apply Online About Carthage Located on the shore of Lake Michigan in the thriving Chicago-Milwaukee corridor, Carthage College blends the best liberal arts traditions with desirable degree programs, transformative learning opportunities, and personal attention from dedicated faculty and staff. Our beautiful campus, an 80-acre arboretum with stunning lake views, is home to 2,600 undergraduate students and 200 graduate students. Founded in 1847, Carthage is consistently named a Best Midwestern College by The Princeton Review and a Most Innovative School by U.S. News & World Report. All Carthage employees play a vital part in the success of our students, as we work together to create an environment where all can achieve their true potential. Grow with Carthage. Carthage College is an equal opportunity employer (EOE) dedicated to the goal of building a culturally diverse community. We welcome applications from a broad spectrum of people, including members of ethnic minorities, women, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender expression, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, protected veteran status or status as an individual with a disability. 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
