    "https://www.carthage.edu/live/news/54010-assistant-professor-chemistry": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Chemistry • Human Resources • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Assistant Professor, Chemistry Home Human Resources Assistant Professor, Chemistry All Stories September 09, 2026 Prof. John Kirk at jkirk1@carthage.edu . Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on LinkedIn Share via Email The Department of Chemistry at Carthage College invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor of biochemistry starting August 2027. We seek a teacher-scholar to contribute to the development of our new Biochemistry major by serving as Program Coordinator, guiding curriculum development, and advising biochemistry students. The successful applicant will be expected to teach biochemistry and general chemistry courses while demonstrating a strong commitment to establishing a productive research program with undergraduates and actively seeking external funding. The Chemistry Department is ACS certified, and our equipment includes a 400-MHz NMR, AFM, HPLC, GC-MS, GC, FTIR, DLS, MP-AES, Fluorimeter, and UV/VIS. The Carthage faculty is firmly committed to the liberal arts tradition and interdisciplinary work. Carthage also offers small class sizes, start-up funds for research, conference travel, and the opportunity to teach, mentor, and advise diverse undergraduates at a liberal arts college. A demonstration of teaching ability will be required at the final interview. More information about the Department may be found at http://www.carthage.edu/chemistry/ . Interested candidates should submit a single PDF file that includes a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, a scholarship statement, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Additional questions about this position can be directed to Prof. John Kirk at jkirk1@carthage.edu. For best consideration, applications should be received by October 16th. Minimum Qualifications Meet all requirements for a Ph.D. in Biochemistry or Chemistry by August 2027 Commitment to innovative curriculum development in chemistry Demonstrated record of or potential for successful undergraduate instruction Demonstrated record of or potential for engagement of undergraduate students in scholarship Enthusiasm for educating students from widely varying backgrounds Apply Online About Carthage Located on the shore of Lake Michigan in the thriving Chicago-Milwaukee corridor, Carthage College blends the best liberal arts traditions with desirable degree programs, transformative learning opportunities, and personal attention from dedicated faculty and staff. Our beautiful campus, an 80-acre arboretum with stunning lake views, is home to 2,600 undergraduate students and 200 graduate students. Founded in 1847, Carthage is consistently named a Best Midwestern College by The Princeton Review and a Most Innovative School by U.S. News & World Report. All Carthage employees play a vital part in the success of our students, as we work together to create an environment where all can achieve their true potential. Grow with Carthage. Carthage College is an equal opportunity employer (EOE) dedicated to the goal of building a culturally diverse community. We welcome applications from a broad spectrum of people, including members of ethnic minorities, women, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender expression, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, protected veteran status or status as an individual with a disability. 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
